      "side": 1,
      "message": "The patch suffers from at least two major problems.\nFirst, the most important, it creates new settings that require the encoder to operate under ultra low bitrates, which degrades video quality significantly. This area is not optimized nor well tested, subject to potential failures causing encoder execution exceptions, rate control problems, or edge reconstruction artifacts.\n\nSecond,the performance metrics, rate-distortion analysis curves, and regression summaries detailed in the documentation plan (extend_cq_level_plan.md) contradict the actual implementation state. IIUC, there are problems in the implementation as shown in other comments. The test output results were either computed against completely unintended fallback code segments or based on detached simulation environments.",
      "revId": "d887253df88be1ff55a41441d6d2a684a59429a5",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
